"Internal Error ()\nciteturn7view0 [wordlim: 200] Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://github.com/pepper-project/giraffe/commits/master/\",\"lineno\":null}); \nFailed to fetch https://github.com/pepper-project/giraffe/commits/master/: Cache miss--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSpeeding Up Sum-Check Proving (Extended Version) (https://eprint.iacr.org/2026/587)\nciteturn7view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: find({\"ref_id\":\"https://eprint.iacr.org/2026/587\",\"pattern\":\"History\"}); Total lines: 82\nL0: # What a lovely hat\nL1: #### Is it made out of 【0†tin foil†iacr.org】?\nL2: \nL3: 【1†Cryptology ePrint Archive】\nL4: \nL5:   * 【2†Papers】 Updates from the last:\nL6:     * 【3†7 days】\nL7:     * 【4†31 days】\nL8:     * 【5†6 months】\nL9:     * 【6†365 days】\nL10:     * * * *\nL11: \nL12:     * 【7†Listing by year】\nL13:     * 【8†All papers】\nL14:     * 【9†Compact view】\nL15:     * 【10†Subscribe†www.iacr.org】\nL16:     * * * *\nL17: \nL18:     * 【11†How to cite】\nL19:     * * * *\nL20:     * 【12†Harvesting metadata】\nL21:   * 【2†Submissions】\nL22:     * 【13†Submit a paper】\nL23:     * 【14†Revise or withdraw a paper】\nL24:     * 【15†Acceptance and publishing conditions】\nL25: \nL26: 【16†Image: Search Button】\nL27: \nL28: [Input] [Button: Search ]\nL29: #### Paper 2026/587\nL30: \nL31: ### 【17†Speeding Up Sum-Check Proving (Extended Version)】\nL32: \nL33: Quang Dao, Carnegie Mellon University\nL34: \nL35: Zachary DeStefano, New York University\nL36: \nL37: Suyash Bagad, Ingonyama\nL38: \nL39: Yuval Domb, Ingonyama\nL40: \nL41: Justin Thaler, Georgetown University, a16z crypto research\nL42: ##### Abstract\nL43: The sum-check protocol is a foundational primitive in modern cryptographic proof systems, but its prover-side cost has emerged as a concrete bottleneck. This paper introduces three complementary techniques that significantly reduce sum-check proving time and memory, especially in the context of zero-knowledge virtual machines (zkVMs).\nL44: First, for applications involving products of many multilinear polynomials, we develop a new algorithm that significantly reduces the number of field multiplications required for proving. Second, we develop a \"small-value sum-check prover\" algorithm. This significantly speeds up the prover in the common setting where the polynomials being summed evaluate to 64 or 32-bit integers, or to elements of a small sub-field within a larger extension field.\nL45: Even outside of the small-value setting, this algorithm yields a faster \"streaming prover\", by which we mean a small-space algorithm that applies whenever the terms being summed can be enumerated in small space (as arises, for example, in zkVM applications). Third, we nearly eliminate prover overhead in the ubiquitous case where one factor is an equality polynomial by exploiting its decomposable tensor structure.\nL46: We implement these techniques in Jolt, a state-of-the-art zkVM, and evaluate their performance. In Jolt, we observe over an order of magnitude runtime speedup and memory reduction on the Spartan sub-protocol, and $1.7\\times$ to $2.2\\times$ speedups for a key high-degree sum-check sub-protocol in the Shout batch-evaluation argument.\nL47: Note: This manuscript directly combines and improves upon results from prior works: 2025/1117, 2024/1046, and 2024/1210\nL48: ##### Metadata\nL49: Available format(s)\nL50:     【17†PDF】\nL51: Category\nL52:     【18†Applications】\nL53: Publication info\nL54:     Preprint.\nL55: Keywords\nL56:     【19†sum-check】【20†snark】【21†zkvm】【22†delayed-reduction】【23†jolt】【24†spartan】【25†twist-shout】\nL57: Contact author(s)\nL58:     qvd @ andrew cmu edu\nL59: zd2131 @ nyu edu\nL60: suyash @ ingonyama com\nL61: yuval domb @ gmail com\nL62: justin r thaler @ gmail com\nL63: History\nL64:     2026-03-25: approved\nL65:     2026-03-24: received\nL66:     【26†See all versions】\nL67: Short URL\nL68:     【27†https://ia.cr/2026/587†ia.cr】\nL69: License\nL70: \nL71: 【28†CC BY†creativecommons.org】\nL72: BibTeX 【29†Image】Copy to clipboard\nL73: \nL74:     @misc{cryptoeprint:2026/587,\nL75:           author = {Quang Dao and Zachary DeStefano and Suyash Bagad and Yuval Domb and Justin Thaler},\nL76:           title = {Speeding Up Sum-Check Proving (Extended Version)},\nL77:           howpublished = {Cryptology {ePrint} Archive, Paper 2026/587},\nL78:           year = {2026},\nL79:           url = {https://eprint.iacr.org/2026/587}\nL80:     }\nL81: Note: In order to protect the privacy of readers, eprint.iacr.org does not use cookies or embedded third party content.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nMore Optimizations to Sum-Check Proving (https://eprint.iacr.org/2024/1210)\nciteturn7view2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: yesterday; Content type: text/html; Source: find({\"ref_id\":\"https://eprint.iacr.org/2024/1210\",\"pattern\":\"History\"}); Total lines: 73\nL0: # What a lovely hat\nL1: #### Is it made out of 【0†tin foil†iacr.org】?\nL2: \nL3: 【1†Cryptology ePrint Archive】\nL4: \nL5:   * 【2†Papers】 Updates from the last:\nL6:     * 【3†7 days】\nL7:     * 【4†31 days】\nL8:     * 【5†6 months】\nL9:     * 【6†365 days】\nL10:     * * * *\nL11: \nL12:     * 【7†Listing by year】\nL13:     * 【8†All papers】\nL14:     * 【9†Compact view】\nL15:     * 【10†Subscribe†www.iacr.org】\nL16:     * * * *\nL17: \nL18:     * 【11†How to cite】\nL19:     * * * *\nL20:     * 【12†Harvesting metadata】\nL21:   * 【2†Submissions】\nL22:     * 【13†Submit a paper】\nL23:     * 【14†Revise or withdraw a paper】\nL24:     * 【15†Acceptance and publishing conditions】\nL25: \nL26: 【16†Image: Search Button】\nL27: \nL28: [Input] [Button: Search ]\nL29: #### Paper 2024/1210\nL30: \nL31: ### 【17†More Optimizations to Sum-Check Proving】\nL32: \nL33: Quang Dao, Carnegie Mellon University\nL34: \nL35: Justin Thaler, Georgetown University, a16z crypto research\nL36: ##### Abstract\nL37: Many fast SNARKs apply the sum-check protocol to an $n$-variate polynomial of the form $g(x) = \\text{eq}(w,x) \\cdot p(x)$, where $p$ is a product of multilinear polynomials, $w \\in \\mathbb{F}^n$ is a random vector, and $\\text{eq}$ is the multilinear extension of the equality function. In this setting, we describe an optimization to the sum-check prover that substantially reduces the cost coming from the $\\text{eq}(w, x)$ factor.\nL38: Our work further improves on a prior optimization by Gruen (ePrint 2023), and in the small-field case, can be combined with additional optimizations by Bagad, Domb, and Thaler (ePrint 2024), and Dao and Thaler (ePrint 2024). Over large prime-order fields, our optimization eliminates roughly $2^{n + 1}$ field multiplications compared to a standard linear-time implementation of the prover, and roughly $2^{n-1}$ field multiplications when considered on top of Gruen's optimization.\nL39: These savings are about a 25% (respectively 10%) end-to-end prover speedup in common use cases, and potentially even larger when working over binary tower fields.\nL40: ##### Metadata\nL41: \nL42: Available format(s)\nL43:     【17†PDF】\nL44: Category\nL45:     【18†Cryptographic protocols】\nL46: Publication info\nL47:     Preprint.\nL48: Keywords\nL49:     【19†sum-check protocol】【20†interactive proofs】【21†SNARKs】\nL50: Contact author(s)\nL51:     justin r thaler @ gmail com\nL52: History\nL53:     2024-07-29: approved\nL54:     2024-07-27: received\nL55:     【22†See all versions】\nL56: Short URL\nL57:     【23†https://ia.cr/2024/1210†ia.cr】\nL58: License\nL59: \nL60: 【24†CC BY†creativecommons.org】\nL61: BibTeX 【25†Image】Copy to clipboard\nL62: \nL63:     @misc{cryptoeprint:2024/1210,\nL64:           author = {Quang Dao and Justin Thaler},\nL65:           title = {More Optimizations to Sum-Check Proving},\nL66:           howpublished = {Cryptology {ePrint} Archive, Paper 2024/1210},\nL67:           year = {2024},\nL68:           url = {https://eprint.iacr.org/2024/1210}\nL69:     }\nL70: \nL71: \nL72: Note: In order to protect the privacy of readers, eprint.iacr.org does not use cookies or embedded third party content.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nTracking: consolidate Akita sumcheck into Jolt and complete native Spongefish integration · Issue #61 · LayerZero-Labs/akita · GitHub (https://github.com/LayerZero-Labs/akita/issues/61)\nciteturn7view3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 4 days ago; Content type: text/html; Source: find({\"ref_id\":\"https://github.com/LayerZero-Labs/akita/issues/61\",\"pattern\":\"opened\"}); Total lines: 299\nL1: ## Navigation Menu\nL2: \nL3: 【1†Sign in】\nL4: \nL5: Appearance settings\nL6: \nL7:   * Platform\nL8: \nL9:     * AI CODE CREATION\nL10:       * 【2†GitHub CopilotWrite better code with AI】\nL11:       * 【3†GitHub Copilot appDirect agents from issue to merge】\nL12:       * 【4†MCP RegistryIntegrate external tools】\nL13: \nL14:     * DEVELOPER WORKFLOWS\nL15:       * 【5†ActionsAutomate any workflow】\nL16:       * 【6†CodespacesInstant dev environments】\nL17:       * 【7†IssuesPlan and track work】\nL18:       * 【8†Code ReviewManage code changes】\nL19:       * 【9†Code QualityEnforce quality at merge】\nL20:     * APPLICATION SECURITY\nL21:       * 【10†GitHub Advanced SecurityFind and fix vulnerabilities】\nL22:       * 【11†Code securitySecure your code as you build】\nL23:       * 【12†Secret protectionStop leaks before they start】\nL24: \nL25:     * EXPLORE\nL26:       * 【13†Why GitHub】\nL27:       * 【14†Documentation†docs.github.com】\nL28:       * 【15†Blog†github.blog】\nL29:       * 【16†Changelog†github.blog】\nL30:       * 【17†Marketplace】\nL31: \nL32: 【18†View all features】\nL33: \nL34:   * Solutions\nL35:     * BY COMPANY SIZE\nL36:       * 【19†Enterprises】\nL37:       * 【20†Small and medium teams】\nL38:       * 【21†Startups】\nL39:       * 【22†Nonprofits】\nL40: \nL41:     * BY USE CASE\nL42:       * 【23†App Modernization】\nL43:       * 【24†DevSecOps】